            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0347" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 351.117/73</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Sharp to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1302. Your 1406, March 4. Foreign Office replies that in France, Louis Levy is
                    French, being born abroad of a French father; that as such he is subject in
                    France to the obligations of military service; and that under these conditions
                    his request does not seem susceptible of favorable action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
